As other people have said, you really do need the magic resistance at
the very least, once you get the Book of the Dead, the Wizard will be
showing up regularly from then until the end of the game, and one of
his tricks is Finger of Death.  It *is* possible to win the game
without it, but it'll be risky, as one inattentive turn could be enough
for him to pop in and zap you with it.

Some ideas:
1. Use the discoveries command (backslash) to find out exactly what
items you still know.  You probably still remember at least a few
things.  If Identify is in that list, then your task is a lot easier
than it could be.
2. Figure out what your wands are using the engrave trick.  Engrave a
few letters with your finger on a spot, then try to add on to the
engraving with each wand in turn.  Most of the important wands will
supply you with special messages.  If the Castle wand of wishing is in
the stack, then it'll give you a wish when you try this, so no need to
worry about wasting it.  Of course, if you remember having a wand of
cancellation beforehand, be careful putting wands into bags.  Best not
to let one tragic event lead to another.  (Wands of Cancellation are
one of three kinds of wands that cause already-existing text to vanish
when you engrave with it.)
3. Wands of Death are among the most useful items you can have in the
late game, since they can kill the Wizard and two of the three riders
relatively quickly.  Don't play around with them until you get magic
resistance or reflection, one of the two, back.
4. Go back up to a shopkeeper and drop scrolls in his shop to get
prices for them.  The cheapest scroll in the game is identify.  Once
you find out what it is, bless all of them you have, drop all known
items onto the ground and have as many unknown items you can't figure
out easily in your inventory, then start reading them.  Sometimes a
blessed scroll of Identify will ID your whole pack, which can be a game
saver in this instance.  If you have magic markers lying around, and
you know what Identify is, that would be a very good thing to write.
5. I hate doing it myself, but in a case like this, price IDing at a
shopkeeper can help out a lot.  Look for the relevant spoilers on the
technique.

Good luck, let us know how it turns out!

